# Data preservation is a release invariant

For every feature, PRD, migration, cleanup or refactor that touches data:
- Read `docs/data-safety/POLICY.md` and complete its change record before editing.
- Preserve original uploads, submitted form answers, signed documents, source
  charts, physician work, lineage, financial records and audit history.
- Never use destructive migrations, replacement inserts, silent truncation,
  age-only deletion, or success responses for unaccounted input.
- Commit business state and durable work/email receipts atomically. Retry must
  recover the same operation without replacing evidence or mixing patients.
- Snapshot all affected stores and blob trees before and after; prove every
  old ID and unchanged value/blob survives. Missing evidence blocks release.
- Test crashes, write failures, retries, partial input and concurrent operations.
- Require independent audit, verified backups and a restore drill before release.
- Authorized legal retention/deletion is a separate, scoped, reviewed procedure;
  an ordinary PRD is never authorization to delete product data.
